  "details": "A new idea for increased avatar customizability is \"keys\" \nImagine parts of the model than you can put your finger onto and activate a function. \nTouch a piano attached to your model and press the keys infront of you to play each individual key sound instead of just playing a song's mp3.\nA dj keyboard that activates lights, smog, and a song without canceling from an accidental gesture press \nA gun infront of you that you can press the release button on the magazine so it drops on the floor, pull a trigger and make it fire, take off the scope and replace it. \n\nIt can be done with pressure sensitivity 0%-100% on a press or a I/0 press\n\nThe idea of having these on avatars would greatly increase what the player can do with these \"keys\", just like how cameras have been a special expansion. Midi and keyboards would be able to expand creativity a step forward. Imagine a full-body streamer player seamlessly controlling the stream with their control deck or a desktop player playing their piano in the pug.",
